## Model card

- **Name:** Gemini 4 Argon
- **Short description:** Google's Gemini 4-generation model, served on OpenCode Zen as `opencode/gemini-4-argon` per this folder's `meta.json` (positioned for long-horizon software engineering, enterprise knowledge work, and defensive cybersecurity). Not listed in any public Google model catalog I could reach.
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/gemini-4-argon` (per `meta.json` in this folder). No OpenRouter listing (`openrouter.ai/google/gemini-4-argon` returns 404). No Google AI Studio / Gemini API / Vertex AI endpoint found.
- **Release / knowledge:** no verified public release date found; not present in the Gemini API changelog through 2026-10-08.
- **IDs:** `opencode/gemini-4-argon` (Zen only, per meta.json; `noFreeId: true` — no Free ID on Zen).
- **Context window:** meta.json (curated, not vendor-verified): "1M total (262K output; 1M via continuation)". No official doc confirms this.
- **Modalities:** meta.json: "Text, image, video in; text out". Not vendor-verified.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-12):** meta.json tiers: "Intro $2.00/$10.00 per 1M in/out", "Standard $4.00/$20.00 per 1M in/out", "Cached input $0.10 per 1M". Not vendor-verified.
- **Architecture:** proprietary; no parameter counts published.

## Negative findings (why no scores)

Research attempted 2026-10-12, minimum three independent source classes, all failing to yield a single verifiable benchmark number:

1. **Official Google docs** — `ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models` model index (fetched 2026-10-12): no Gemini 4 / Argon entry; latest Gemini family listed is 3.8 (3.8 Flash, 3.8 Live, 3.8 Flash TTS, 3.5/3.6 Flash, 3.1/2.5 tiers). Model page `ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models/gemini-4-argon` → HTTP 404. Vertex AI model catalog (`cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/models`, fetched 2026-10-12): no Gemini 4 / Argon; newest generative entries are Gemini 3.8 Flash / 3.8 Flash Cyber / 3.8 Live. Gemini API changelog (through 2026-10-08 entry, fetched 2026-10-12): no Gemini 4 or Argon mention in the visible October entries. Google blog product page: no model data extractable.
2. **Independent benchmark trackers** — Artificial Analysis model page `artificialanalysis.ai/models/gemini-4-argon` EXISTS (title "Gemini 4 Argon (high)", fetched directly and via text-render proxy 2026-10-12) but every metric (Intelligence Index v4.3.2, AA-Briefcase Elo, GDPval-AA, Terminal-Bench 4.0, SciCode, HLE, GDP.pdf, CritPt, AA-Omniscience, AA-LCR, pricing, context window) renders client-side only — zero numeric values extractable from static HTML. AA public data API: no accessible endpoint (404).
3. **Aggregators / gateways** — OpenRouter `google/gemini-4-argon`: 404 (via text proxy, fetched 2026-10-12). LMArena leaderboard: empty response. Web search tool: backend 404 throughout the session (retried multiple times). DuckDuckGo HTML endpoint: bot-challenge wall.

**Conclusion:** the only traceable public artifact is the Artificial Analysis page's existence (proving the model is tracked somewhere as "Gemini 4 Argon (high)") plus the Zen route in `meta.json`. No benchmark value, price, context limit, or modality spec could be independently verified from a fetchable source. Per the self-exclusion rule (template + `tasks/research.md`), a scored file would require inventing every number — forbidden. Saved as `.md.excluded` notes; `pnpm sync` ignores scores herein.

